Migratory Birds

Given an array of integers where each element represents a bird type id, determine the id of the most frequently sighted bird type.

If more than one bird type has the same highest frequency, return the smallest bird type id among them.

Example
arr = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3]

Bird sightings:

Type 1 → 2 times
Type 2 → 2 times
Type 3 → 1 time

Both type 1 and type 2 appear the most (2 times).
Return the smaller id, which is:

1
Function Description

Complete the function:

migratoryBirds(List<Integer> arr)
Parameter

arr[n] : a list of integers representing the bird type ids sighted

Returns

int : the lowest bird type id of the most frequently sighted birds.

Input Format

The first line contains an integer n, the size of the array.

The second line contains n space-separated integers, each representing a bird type id.

Constraints
5 ≤ n ≤ 2 × 10^5
Each bird type id is one of: 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5
Sample Input
6
1 4 4 4 5 3
Sample Output
4